# Build-time, non-secret configuration. Copy to `.env` for local overrides; set
# the same values as plain environment variables on the Cloudflare build.
#
# Everything here is public: PUBLIC_ vars are inlined into the page, and the two
# addresses are visible in the mail they produce. Secrets live in `.dev.vars`
# locally and in Worker secrets in production — never here.
#
# All of these have working defaults in `astro.config.mjs`, so this file is only
# needed to override one.

# The Turnstile *site* key. Public — it renders into the widget markup. Defaults
# to Blinto's real widget, so production needs no build variable at all.
#
# Set this locally to Cloudflare's always-passes test key if the real widget's
# hostname list does not include localhost. Its matching test secret, for
# `.dev.vars`, is 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA.
# PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="1x00000000000000000000AA"

# Where enquiries are delivered.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL="hello@blinto.co"

# The sender. Must be an address on a domain verified in Resend.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL="Blinto <noreply@blinto.co>"

# For a deliberate local production build against the Turnstile test pair, the
# output check needs an explicit opt-out. It reads the real environment, not
# this file, so pass it on the command line:
#   ALLOW_TURNSTILE_TEST_KEY=1 npm run build
